WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:01.640
- Hi, I'm Angie.

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:02.870
- Hi, I'm Sarah.

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:04.820
- We're the winners of
the Jubilee Sweepstakes.

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:06.940
- Hope you enjoy this video.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.680
- The specific thing
of doing it to a child

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.210
that has no say is something I kinda.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.650
- The same way is becoming a Jew.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:14.700
We have no say.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.600
- Yeah, but becoming a Jew
doesn't necessarily mean

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.233
doing something to your private parts.

00:00:20.233 --> 00:00:22.650
(cool music)

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.270
- [Moderator] Step forward if you agree,

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:37.193
Jewish men should be circumcised.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.003
- This is part of my
relationship with God,

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:50.000
but I don't understand
why the rest of the world

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:50.890
would do it.

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:52.460
I do it because God says,

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:54.940
this is my relationship with you do this.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:57.240
And I will be your God forever.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.240
When God says to me, circumcise
your son at eight days,

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:03.460
I do it because that is what Jews do.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:05.110
- I remember hearing a story of a woman

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:07.480
who was on a transport to Auschwitz.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:09.860
She had just given birth to a baby boy.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.070
And while she was marching,

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:14.210
she asked someone for a knife

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:16.640
and the German soldier
mocked her and said,

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:17.526
you wanna make your,

00:01:17.526 --> 00:01:21.070
you wanna bring an end
to your life sooner.

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:23.610
And apparently she took the knife,

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:27.070
circumcised her son with the comments

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:29.170
so that he should die a jew.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:34.170
These types of images create
such burning metaphors

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:38.000
that our families, our grandparents,

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.070
will sacrifice their lives
under horrible conditions

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:45.650
to be able to maintain that
commandment of circumcision.

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:48.950
- For 3,800 years, we Jews have done this.

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:52.230
It's only been in the last maybe 20 years

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:55.310
that people are starting to
say, well, do we have to do it?

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:59.660
The moment you stop
physically doing the covenant

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:02.453
and the religious things,
assimilation comes in.

00:02:03.613 --> 00:02:05.610
- [Moderator] Can the
disagreers step forward?

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.580
- I just didn't feel it
was appropriate for me

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:11.890
to talk about this because this
is specifically a man issue.

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:14.180
- I'm circumcised and it's never been,

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:15.610
you know an issue for me.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:17.520
Like I never like, oh, I
wish I wasn't circumcised.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:18.590
You know it's whatever.

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:20.660
I don't remember it so, I have, I guess,

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.340
some qualms with it about
doing that to a baby

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:25.000
when they have no say
obviously if you're an adult

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.440
and you wanna do it more
power to you go for it.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:29.650
But the specific thing
of doing it to a child

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:32.386
that has no say is something I kinda.

00:02:32.386 --> 00:02:34.640
- The same way is becoming a Jew.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:35.660
We have no say.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:38.380
- Yeah, but becoming a
Jew doesn't necessarily

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:41.170
mean doing something
to your private parts.

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:42.160
- This is what God wants.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:45.000
This is the first thing
that our father Abraham

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.430
was told by God to do.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:47.990
- When God first asked us to do it,

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:50.620
yes Abraham, who then
could say yes, all right,

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:51.453
I will do that.

00:02:51.453 --> 00:02:52.850
- He would have done
it at eight days also,

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:55.270
but God didn't bring
it up until he was 99.

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:58.310
(contestants laughing)

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:00.290
Hi, my name is Rabbi Chaim.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:02.150
I am on the Orthodox side.

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:04.150
I don't believe there's a God.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.550
I don't believe in Judaism.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:10.550
Belief means that I accept
it, because you say so.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:12.270
I know there's a God.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.081
I know my Judaism is real.

00:03:14.081 --> 00:03:15.300
This is the way God created me.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.550
This is my purpose.

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:20.630
I'm oozing Judaism whether
you recognize it or not.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:22.330
This is who I am.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:26.628
- I don't really believe in a
lot of the religious aspects

00:03:26.628 --> 00:03:30.030
of being Jewish, but I
do love to celebrate,

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:31.390
the holidays with my family.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:33.910
It's sort of more of
a state of being to me

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:37.043
than something I actually do.

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:42.563
- [Moderator] Women and men
have separate roles in society.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:49.950
- Not necessarily that we're
not equal in a certain way,

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:52.460
but especially when it comes to Judaism.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.030
A woman historically has always been

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:56.760
on a higher spiritual level than men.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:00.660
We are the ones that instill the values,

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:02.780
the holiness, the culture.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:05.660
We are very strongly a
part of the community.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:07.350
And it's important that
I'm saying this because

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.790
these little TV shows that come out,

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:10.610
they like to paint the whole situation

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:13.810
as if Orthodox Jewish women
are second class citizens

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:15.780
and they just wanna leave the community.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:17.267
And it's so hard for them to exist

00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:19.287
and they have no saying and no life.

00:04:19.287 --> 00:04:20.550
And it's not true.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:22.760
- I don't go around saying, well,

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:25.650
we're totally equal in all areas.

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:29.710
I have different
responsibilities when I pray,

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:30.870
because like you said,

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:35.460
my soul needs greater
rectification to reach holiness.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.700
Whereas my wife's soul, it's a local call,

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:40.790
for me it's a long distance call,

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:42.834
but we have different roles.

00:04:42.834 --> 00:04:46.050
- I want to feel equal in
all aspects of Judaism.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:49.730
And all you have to do is
go to the Kotel in Jerusalem

00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:52.730
and take a step back and look
at where the (indistinct) is,

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:55.510
where the divider is between
men and women at the wall.

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:57.750
And the men have three
quarters of the wall.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:01.680
The women have a quarter and
we're all packed in there.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:05.026
And I wanted to have my time
to touch the Kotel and pray.

00:05:05.026 --> 00:05:07.257
And I'm trying to, you
know have that moment.

00:05:07.257 --> 00:05:10.660
And it was really hard
to not have that moment

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:11.710
when I was there.

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:15.830
- God did create a male
and female for a purpose.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:19.680
If he wanted us all to be
the same way of practice,

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:21.440
then we would've been exactly the same.

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:23.190
- God created six other genders as well,

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:24.173
which are also in-

00:05:24.173 --> 00:05:26.010
- We'll get to that, we'll
get to that in a moment.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:29.100
God says, I don't trust men
because women are holier.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:33.720
- I've heard that narrative a
lot of how women are holier.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:35.930
I think the biggest thing
for me is if a woman

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:38.839
wants to wear a Kippah or a Tallis,

00:05:38.839 --> 00:05:42.110
she feels like it makes her closer to God,

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:44.373
why should she not be allowed to do that?

00:05:44.373 --> 00:05:46.237
I think that's my biggest issue.

00:05:46.237 --> 00:05:47.670
- Add that to your Kosher.

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:50.390
Add that to the Mikvah,
in every religious home,

00:05:50.390 --> 00:05:53.440
the woman is seriously on a pedestal.

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:56.500
- In theory, that
sounds, that sounds good.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:59.890
But I think in practice, men are you know

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:02.710
praying a certain way to,
to feel closer to God.

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:05.490
And when women want to do
that, they are told they can't.

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:06.970
- I just wanna step in for a second.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:09.260
I wanna say, even though I
do believe what I believe.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:12.330
I still believe that if
people want to do something,

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:13.430
they have the right to do so,

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:16.060
and I'm not gonna judge them for it.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.923
- [Moderator] I would only
marry a Jewish person.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.530
- I married somebody Jewish

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:30.510
and I wouldn't have thought
of going out with anyone else

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:32.470
because marriage is not about love.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:36.890
I'm here to build the next
generation of Jewish people.

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:39.820
I'm on a mission as a Jew
to keep Judaism alive.

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:43.330
- Marrying a Jew is of
paramount importance to me,

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:45.300
primarily because I see what happens

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:49.200
to many intermarried
couples down the road.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.440
Where I see the fights that creep up come

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:52.890
Christmas Hanukkah time.

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:57.800
Statistically, the divorce rate
is so high in this country.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:01.670
So why go into a relationship
where you have statistical

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:04.180
obstacles to prevent you
from ultimately having

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:05.400
a healthy marriage?

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:07.350
- Because I grew up in
a reformed synagogue.

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:09.790
We're very accepting of
different interfaith families

00:07:09.790 --> 00:07:10.800
and things like that.

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:12.880
I mean, definitely is possible, but again,

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:15.850
in all different walks of
life, different sex of Judaism,

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:17.040
it's so different.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:19.053
- So the couples that you are aware of

00:07:19.053 --> 00:07:22.350
that were successful
in their intermarriage,

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:25.720
what happened to their children
and specifically were the

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:26.830
mothers Jewish or not?

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:29.650
If the mothers were not
Jewish, under Jewish law,

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:31.000
the kids are not Jewish.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.920
- The couples I know are still together.

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:34.210
Some of them, the mothers Jewish,

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:35.450
some of them, the fathers Jewish,

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:37.790
there are more progressive
values coming up

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.940
that say that, you know
if your father's Jewish,

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:42.020
we'll still accept you into the community

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:45.560
because we want as many Jews
into the community as possible.

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.720
Obviously not always successful,

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:51.703
but I have seen those successful
circumstances for sure.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:58.080
I'm Aly, I'm here as a secular Jew.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.240
And I identify as a reform Jew.

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:04.090
I have dated a non-Jewish
person once or twice,

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:07.270
and it's something that
my parents didn't love.

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:10.460
And I actually kept one
parts of it a secret

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:11.760
for a little bit.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:14.280
This is the one area where
it's really important

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:17.080
for them to, for me to end
up with a Jewish partner

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:20.100
because again, raising Jewish families

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:22.340
and celebrating holidays together

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:24.480
it just minimizes conflict.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:27.330
I just find a lot of connection
with other Jewish people.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:31.580
- Just being Jewish
isn't enough for me to,

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:35.100
be in, oh well, that's someone
I wanna spend my life with.

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:37.923
My dad, who is Jewish.

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:40.870
When he started dating my
mom and when he married her,

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:43.180
they were, my mom was raised Christian

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:44.013
and she wasn't Jewish.

00:08:44.013 --> 00:08:45.060
She did convert later.

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:47.340
They married and it was
an interfaith couple

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:48.810
for like a couple years.

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:50.560
- Every person who I've dated

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:52.960
or who's ever loved me
has not been Jewish.

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:55.830
And I mainly attracted the
people who aren't Jewish

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:57.323
because I grew up Jewish.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:01.120
I'm Yoanna like Moana,

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:01.997
my pronouns are she, they.

00:09:01.997 --> 00:09:06.820
I'm 20 and I am a secular Jew.

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:09.460
My family was Orthodox.

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:14.290
I feel judged by Orthodox Jews a lot

00:09:14.290 --> 00:09:16.540
because I'm queer presenting.

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:18.370
I found it very restricting.

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:20.170
Now being the kind of
Jew that I get to be,

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:22.733
it's a lot more freeing, I get to be me.

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:26.720
- [Moderator] I support
Israel in its conflict

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:27.793
with Palestine.

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:31.763
Oh boy.

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.410
- Israel deserves to exist.

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:37.860
Israel is our ancestral homeland.

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:41.470
Also Jewish liberation doesn't
have to come at the cost

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:44.640
of Palestinians losing their freedom.

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:47.980
So in that sense, I don't
agree with the last part of it.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:50.660
However, the conflict is
a different situation.

00:09:50.660 --> 00:09:51.493
- Like you were saying,

00:09:51.493 --> 00:09:54.380
it shouldn't have to come at
the expense of Palestinians.

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:56.720
There is a conflict going
on right there right now.

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:57.860
What's true for us is different

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:00.490
than what's true for other people.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:03.070
And we should just be
able to live in peace.

00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:03.903
I know we want that.

00:10:03.903 --> 00:10:08.314
- I think blind support for
anything is problematic.

00:10:08.314 --> 00:10:09.147
- Yes.

00:10:09.147 --> 00:10:11.160
I'm Canadian, do I support every action

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:12.790
the Canadian government takes?

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:13.623
No.

00:10:13.623 --> 00:10:15.560
Do I support Canada?

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:16.393
Of course.

00:10:16.393 --> 00:10:17.226
- Okay.

00:10:17.226 --> 00:10:18.059
I'm going to say something

00:10:18.059 --> 00:10:19.430
that's most probably going to explode

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:20.900
this entire conversation.

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:24.370
1947 there was no such
thing as Palestinian people.

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:27.050
They were Jordanians or Egyptian citizens,

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:31.630
in 1948 these Jordanian
and Egyptian citizens

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:35.100
were told by their people
go into refugee camps

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:37.620
we'll wipe out the Jewish
people and you'll move back.

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:40.630
In 1964 Yasser Arafat came out and said,

00:10:40.630 --> 00:10:43.470
I am going to raise up a people

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:45.460
and call them the Palestinians.

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:48.270
'Cause we are going to liberate
Palestine from the Jews.

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:49.150
The question was,

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:54.150
do I support the conflict
between Israel and Palestine?

00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:59.860
I really don't, because the
Palestine never existed.

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:01.635
- My issue with it is that
you just don't see them

00:11:01.635 --> 00:11:02.718
as a people, but that's not-

00:11:02.718 --> 00:11:03.612
- No, no, no.

00:11:03.612 --> 00:11:04.770
I didn't say, the Jordanian,

00:11:04.770 --> 00:11:06.300
why didn't the Jordanians take them in?

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:08.190
Why didn't the Egyptians
take in their citizens?

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:10.930
- I, don't know why that
happened, but regardless,

00:11:10.930 --> 00:11:13.310
a Palestinian people-hood was created

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:14.779
and we can't take that away.

00:11:14.779 --> 00:11:17.140
- But terrorism comes from it.

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:18.580
- Terrorism can come from anywhere.

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:20.030
We have it in our own country.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:20.980
- I'd like to comment,

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:23.930
you know I'm a little sick
and tired of the rhetoric

00:11:23.930 --> 00:11:27.380
where American Jews have to
apologize with this proviso,

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:31.030
by saying that Israel has
a right to defend itself,

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:32.610
Israel has a right to exist.

00:11:32.610 --> 00:11:35.900
You don't hear that language anywhere.

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:40.200
No, proud citizen of
any country says America

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:41.320
has the right to exist.

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:42.770
England has the right to exist.

00:11:42.770 --> 00:11:44.200
Do I have to justify it?

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:48.000
Do I have to bend over backwards
to gain the recognition

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:51.310
and the acceptance of those who
are sitting there like this,

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:52.200
judging me.

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:53.033
I won't.

00:11:53.033 --> 00:11:55.340
- There is always this
binary terminology also

00:11:55.340 --> 00:11:56.950
that's used as very destructive.

00:11:56.950 --> 00:12:00.550
There is are you
pro-Palestinian or pro-Israel?

